==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|decem||ten|lang=la}} + {{term|annum||year|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪˈsɛnɪəm/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|decenniums|decennia}}

# A period of ten years.
#* {{quote-newsgroup|year=1998|passage=G.B. still has to cope with the heritage of approx. 20 years of consecutive Conservative reigns, just as you guys are getting your act together after almost a '''decennium''' of Enlightened Ronnie.|url=http://groups.google.com./group/soc.culture.netherlands/msg/016a12814629ba81|newsgroup=soc.culture.netherlands}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|year=1996|passage=Christian leaders refused even to *look* through Galileo's telescope (as a matter of fact, the Vatican cleared Galileo's name only as late as in the previous '''decennium''').|url=http://groups.google.com./group/soc.culture.usa/msg/349c19c9a5ca84fd|newsgroup=soc.culture.usa}}

